I liked the first game so I was keen to play the second. I love the visual style: everything looks rough and sketchy, as though drawn with a pencil. The humour and creepiness are still there, and there's room for another sequel (though I suspect this is unlikely, given how much time has passed since release).
A couple of minuses that you should be aware of:
* I found some of the explanations of the rules for some puzzles so vague that I genuinely did not know what they were getting at until I asked for a hint;
* I encountered a couple of bugs where certain elements on the screen were blacked out (restarting my PC rectified this - fortunately there is autosave so only a little progress was lost);
* some of the puzzles aren't as user-friendly as I would have expected, like I was fighting to move/drag puzzle elements (perhaps I wasn't quite clicking them right?).
Despite these issues, I still recommend this game, particularly if you get it in a bundle or on sale. Have fun!

LISA is an RPG that is reminiscent of earthbound. It has a pain full but memorable soundtrack that has a large catalog. LISA has a refreshing take on turn based combat and it all happens in a dark depressing post-apocalyptic world. The game excels at making the player agonize at every choice they make. The narrative is not afraid of normal taboos and explores them thoroughly. I would recommend this game to people who love Off or absurd games that step into dark themes.
