At first glance the game is wonderfull. it has an intuitive interface, multiplayer (
), interesting landscapes and more. The game sets you off with a settler and a warrior. You start off on turn 1, enable automatic turn end and suddenly its 4 am and you are at war with three nations. Very time consuming, hence every other review including mine starting with "Just one more turn".
The game is heavily dependant on microtransactions to be enjoyable. Not every DLC is expensive but if you want to experience the full Civilization experience, you are going to thank yourself for buying the DLC's.

